WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.454
Progress is not vibes.

00:00:01.454 --> 00:00:03.634
Progress is evidence you can show.

00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:06.178
This lesson is about evidence of progress.

00:00:06.178 --> 00:00:07.995
What counts as weekly proof.

00:00:07.995 --> 00:00:10.539
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:10.539 --> 00:00:14.174
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:14.174 --> 00:00:19.625
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:19.625 --> 00:00:23.623
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:27.984
Stay practical: list three evidence metrics before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:28.304 --> 00:00:34.686
Weekly proof looks like conversations started, offers sent, money asked, and lessons shipped with a quiz pass.

00:00:34.686 --> 00:00:37.314
Remember the objective: list three evidence metrics.

00:00:37.314 --> 00:00:41.444
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:41.444 --> 00:00:45.949
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:45.949 --> 00:00:50.079
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:50.079 --> 00:00:54.584
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:54.904 --> 00:00:58.240
List three evidence metrics you will track this month.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.463
Keep them countable without a dashboard.

00:01:00.463 --> 00:01:03.058
Remember the objective: list three evidence metrics.

00:01:03.058 --> 00:01:07.135
